{
  "about": "A real head of this repository whose held-back suites skipped: cybermonklabs/legion's head 4198cda5fd0ae76e055089846f40f7be0d10dcf4, of pull request #4464. checkRuns are GitHub's 54 check runs on that head under 53 names, pr-title having run twice, as gh api --paginate \"repos/cybermonklabs/legion/commits/4198cda5fd0ae76e055089846f40f7be0d10dcf4/check-runs?filter=all&per_page=100\" --jq '[.check_runs[] | {id, name, status, conclusion, started_at, completed_at, html_url, head_sha, app: {id: .app.id}}]' answered it; 28 of them concluded skipped and 26 success. settlement is the settlement Envoy's listener publishes for them once every run has completed, in the shape listener-rules.json writes one: each check's highest-id run, so pr-title's later run alone, each check_runs entry carrying that run's conclusion word as GitHub gave it, the skipped group naming the 28 skipped checks, the passed group naming the other 25, and no check failed or cancelled. The listing names no pull request, so the listener's test (packages/envoy/internal/cistore, TestTheListenerSettlesACapturedHeadAsItsFixtureSays) delivers each run as its check_run webhook on pull request 4464 through the listener's webhook handler. The fixture holds check runs alone: the command lists no commit status.",
